  "live_records": {
    "q-83754": {
      "dom_id": "step-q83754",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?",
      "worked_solution": "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=2y(500-y).\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=2,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=500.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-83754-a",
